#!grafli v1
# Hydraulics 101 — reveal storyboard
# Companion board to paper.md. Purpose: teaching — so this board is a
# STORYBOARD: one node per beat, in reveal order, mirroring the guided flow
# `wheel-basics` in Sandbox.qml exactly (same order, same vocabulary).
# Started 2026-09-02. If the flow gains or loses a step, this board changes
# in the same commit - the flow is the primary artifact and this is its map.

# ── entry ──
@ box paper "Paper →\nthe lesson plan" 60,60 220x80 %soft &link:./paper.md
@ note legend 900,60 """
press T in the lab
this board is that tour
""" ~small

# ── what they arrive with ──
@ box belief "THE BELIEF THEY ARRIVE WITH\n\"the pump decides how much\nwater flows - the pipe just\ncarries it\"" 60,230 300x150 %accent &link:./paper.md#the-misconception-it-targets

# ── the beats, in reveal order ──
@ box beat1 "1-4 the parts\npump 40 kPa · wheel · narrow pipe 8 kPa·s/L\nflow steps: empty, pump, wheel, pipe" 440,200 280x130 %primary &link:./paper.md#the-demonstration-sequence
@ box beat2 "5 plumbed, valve shut\nnothing moves\nflow step: plumb" 440,360 280x110 %primary &link:./paper.md#the-demonstration-sequence
@ box beat3 "6 THEY open the valve\nflow step: open" 440,500 280x100 %teal &link:./paper.md#the-demonstration-sequence
@ box beat4 "7-9 it turns: 1.18 L/s, everywhere\nwhy: 40 kPa ÷ everything in the loop\nV: the drops sum to the head\nflow steps: turning, why, values" 440,630 280x150 %primary &link:./paper.md#the-demonstration-sequence
@ box beat5 "10 THEY narrow the pipe\nless flow, slower wheel\nflow step: try" 440,810 280x110 %teal &link:./paper.md#the-demonstration-sequence

# ── the moment ──
@ box moment "THE NUMBER THAT CONTRADICTS IT\nseries: 0.80 L/s for both wheels\nparallel: 2.85 L/s, 1.43 each,\nand the pump sags to 34.3 kPa" 780,440 300x160 %rose &link:./paper.md#the-moment-the-number-contradicts-the-belief

# ── the takeaway ──
@ box takeaway "the takeaway\n\"a pump holds a pressure;\nthe loop decides the flow\"" 780,660 300x120 %highlight &link:./paper.md#the-takeaway

# ── the analogy, for the reader who has met copper ──
@ box analogy "the same lesson as electronics-101\nkPa ↔ V · L/s ↔ A · kPa·s/L ↔ Ω\nkPa·L/s = W, no factor" 780,220 300x120 %soft &link:./paper.md#when-they-ask

# ── arrows ──
@ arrow belief -> beat1 "start here"
@ arrow beat1 -> beat2
@ arrow beat2 -> beat3
@ arrow beat3 -> beat4
@ arrow beat4 -> beat5
@ arrow beat4 -> moment "then the presets"
@ arrow moment -> takeaway
@ arrow moment -> belief "revises" !dashed
@ arrow analogy -> takeaway !dashed

# ── the lab itself ──
@ note scen 60,480 """
scenarios (keys 1-4)
1 wheel-basic - one loop, 1.18 L/s
2 series - two wheels, 0.80 L/s
3 parallel - two branches, 2.85 L/s
4 metering - flow meter in line, gauge across
""" ~small &link:./paper.md#measured-results

@ note keys 60,700 """
keys
1-4 presets · T tour · Space next · ← back
C clear · E eraser · V values · Q plot
R turn · # grid · Del remove · f jump
⇧F frame · 0 reset · Shift+R record · ? all
""" ~small &link:./paper.md#how-to-run-it
